From 1ec6ede6270eee226816dde4d7f4b56eaa2c12e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bound the slot index of a trade request

LINKCMD_READY_TO_TRADE carries the slot to trade in a word from the GBA,
and tradePkmnAtIndex() used it unchecked: subspan(index * 100, 100) on
the 600-byte parties, so an index of 6 or more read past the partner's
party and wrote past ours. Games only send 0-5; a corrupted link word or
a homebrew ROM does not have to. Ignore an index outside the party.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014LvpUYFw94JkaNFyrbwJmK
---
 src/payloads/pokemon.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/payloads/pokemon.cpp b/src/payloads/pokemon.cpp
index 819dffa..91d2028 100644
--- a/src/payloads/pokemon.cpp
+++ b/src/payloads/pokemon.cpp
@@ -103,6 +103,9 @@ namespace party
 
     void tradePkmnAtIndex(uint8_t index)
     {
+        // The index comes from the GBA's link word: anything past the party
+        // would read past the partner's and write past ours.
+        if (index >= numberOfSlots) return;
         std::ranges::copy(std::span(g_partnerParty).subspan(index * 100, 100), slot(index).begin());
     }
 
